# A left press anywhere in the gutter of a file nothing can debug — the
# line number, not only the sign cell — selects that line and parks the
# cursor at its column 1 (the line-numbers convention; Rust's gutter
# press fires SelectLineToEnd). Tree off at 120x40: the gutter is
# columns 0–4, the body starts at row 2.
write doc.txt "ED01\nED02\nED03\nED04\nED05\n"
open doc.txt
command view.toggle_tree
expect screen contains "Ln 1/5 Col 1"
# The number cell of line 3 (row 4).
click 3 4
expect screen contains "Ln 3/5 Col 1"
expect screen contains "Sel 5"
# The sign cell of line 5 does the same on a .txt.
click 0 6
expect screen contains "Ln 5/5 Col 1"
expect screen contains "Sel 5"
# No breakpoint was set by either press.
expect screen lacks "breakpoint set"
